<title>USA: Exxon to cut 150 jobs at Florham Park, N.J.</title>
<headline>Exxon to cut 150 jobs at Florham Park, N.J.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Exxon Corp's Exxon International Co is to cut 150 of a total of 600 jobs at the group's headquarters in Florham Park, N.J., a spokeswoman for the company said.</p>
<p>&quot;Exxon International today announced a special program of severance allowances to assist in its ongoing restructuring and resultant need to reduce staffing at its headquarters location,&quot; the spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The division is responsible for most of Exxon's oil and gas exploration outside the U.S. and Canada.</p>
<p>The spokeswoman said that the voluntary phase of the program would run to June 2 and if the required numbers are not achieved, a compulsory program will start.</p>
<p>((-- David Chance New York Newsroom 212 859 1902))</p>
